^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^CONVERSION ERROR$
template scope 'rebind' is ambiguous
--
Regression for [class.member.lookup]/1 + [temp.names]/3: a
nested-template member (`rebind<_Up>`) declared in a derived
class hides a same-named member inherited from any base class.

Previously CBMC's `disambiguate_template_classes` found both
`std::__new_allocator<T>::rebind` and `std::allocator<T>::rebind`
as primary candidates for the `_Tp::template rebind<_Up>` lookup
inside libstdc++'s `std::__alloc_rebind` and errored out with
  template scope 'rebind' is ambiguous

Fix applies the class-inheritance dominance rule: when multiple
primary template candidates have the same base_name, drop any
candidate whose declaring class is a (transitive) base of
another candidate's declaring class.  Here `__new_allocator<T>`
is a base of `allocator<T>` so `__new_allocator::rebind` is
dropped, leaving `allocator<T>::rebind` as the unique match.

Distilled from dog-fooding `goto-cc` on CBMC's own
`src/util/string_container.h`:
  typedef std::unordered_map<string_ptrt, unsigned, string_ptr_hash>
      hash_tablet;
